  "domain": "robotics",
  "definition": "In robotics, acceleration is the rate of change of velocity with respect to time, expressed for each joint (joint-space acceleration) or for the robot's end-effector (task-space acceleration), measured in rad/s\u00b2 or m/s\u00b2 respectively. Acceleration profiles govern the dynamic forces and torques that a manipulator must generate, coupling directly into Newton-Euler equations of motion. Limiting acceleration is central to safety (reducing impact forces) and to trajectory smoothness in collaborative applications.",
